From 8d5cbe8b92fbbe72b6d8fc92bb9ea104c71f4d70 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:49:12 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(setup): a machine or post picked on one setup never
 re-mounts another

With two or more setups, a machine verb (library pick, Load other,
Edit apply, Clear, catalogue assign, mode switch) or a post pick on a
setup that follows the document now makes the pick that setup's own
(SetSetupMachine / SetSetupPost, undoable) instead of writing the
document's mount every other following setup reads. One setup keeps
writing the document's machine as before. The setup's Machine and Post
pages say by name where a pick lands.

Fixes #1515

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL
